# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Do you see advantages to amplitude encoding over basis encoding? If so, explain.\n"
msgstr "Adakah anda nampak kelebihan pengekodan amplitud berbanding pengekodan basis? Jika ada, terangkan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There may be several answers. One answer is that, given the fixed ordering of the basis states, this amplitude encoding preserves the order of the numbers encoded. It will often also be encoded more densely.\n"
msgstr "Mungkin ada beberapa jawapan. Satu jawapan ialah, dengan susunan tetap keadaan basis, pengekodan amplitud ini mengekalkan susunan nombor yang dikodkan. Ia juga sering dikodkan dengan lebih padat.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: Kelebihan
# pengekodan amplitud ialah hanya $\log_2(N)$ qubit
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"A benefit of amplitude encoding is that only $\\log_2(N)$ qubits are required for an $N$-dimensional ($N$-feature) data vector $\\vec{x}\\rightarrow|\\vec{x}\\rangle$. However, amplitude encoding is generally an inefficient procedure that requires arbitrary state preparation, which is exponential in the number of CNOT gates. Stated differently, the state preparation has a polynomial runtime complexity of $\\mathcal O(N)$ in the number of dimensions, where $N = 2^n$, and $n$ is the number of qubits. Amplitude encoding “provides an exponential saving in space at the cost of an exponential increase in time”[\\[3\\]](#references); however, runtime increases to $\\mathcal O(\\log N)$ are achievable in certain cases[\\[4\\]](#references). For an end-to-end quantum speedup, the data loading runtime complexity needs to be considered.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Angle encoding {#angle-encoding}"
msgstr "Pengekodan sudut {#angle-encoding}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Angle encoding is of interest in many QML models using Pauli feature maps such as quantum support vector machines (QSVMs) and variational quantum circuits (VQCs), among others. Angle encoding is closely related to phase encoding and dense angle encoding which are presented below. Here we will use \"angle encoding\" to refer to a rotation in $\\theta$, that is, a rotation away from the $z$ axis accomplished for example by an $R_X$ gate or an $R_Y$ gate[\\[1,3\\]](#references). Really, one can encode data in *any* rotation or combination of rotations. But $R_Y$ is common in the literature, so we emphasize it here.\n"
msgstr "Pengekodan sudut mendapat perhatian dalam banyak model QML yang menggunakan peta ciri Pauli seperti mesin vektor sokongan kuantum (QSVM) dan litar kuantum variatif (VQC), antara lain. Pengekodan sudut berkait rapat dengan pengekodan fasa dan pengekodan sudut padat yang dibentangkan di bawah. Di sini kami akan menggunakan \"pengekodan sudut\" untuk merujuk kepada putaran dalam $\\theta$, iaitu putaran jauh dari paksi $z$ yang dicapai misalnya oleh get $R_X$ atau get $R_Y$[\\[1,3\\]](#references). Sebenarnya, seseorang boleh mengekodkan data dalam *mana-mana* putaran atau gabungan putaran. Tetapi $R_Y$ adalah lazim dalam kesusasteraan, jadi kami menekankannya di sini.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When applied to a single qubit, angle encoding imparts a Y-axis rotation proportional to the data value. Consider the encoding of a single ($k^\\text{th}$)feature from the $j^\\text{th}$ data vector in a dataset, $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k$:\n"
msgstr "Apabila digunakan pada satu qubit tunggal, pengekodan sudut memberikan putaran paksi-Y yang berkadar dengan nilai data. Pertimbangkan pengekodan satu ciri ke-$k$ dari vektor data ke-$j$ dalam set data, $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k\\rangle = R_Y(\\theta=\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|0\\rangle = \\textstyle\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k}{2}\\right)|0\\rangle + \\sin\\left(\\frac{\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k}{2}\\right)|1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k\\rangle = R_Y(\\theta=\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|0\\rangle = \\textstyle\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k}{2}\\right)|0\\rangle + \\sin\\left(\\frac{\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k}{2}\\right)|1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatively, angle encoding can be performed using $R_X(\\theta)$ gates, although the encoded state would have a complex relative phase compared to $R_Y(\\theta)$.\n"
msgstr "Sebagai alternatif, pengekodan sudut boleh dilakukan menggunakan get $R_X(\\theta)$, walaupun keadaan yang dikodkan akan mempunyai fasa relatif kompleks berbanding $R_Y(\\theta)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Angle encoding is different from the previous two methods discussed in several ways. In angle encoding:\n"
"- Each feature value is mapped to a corresponding qubit, $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k \\rightarrow Q_k$, leaving the qubits in a product state.\n"
"- One numerical value is encoded at a time, rather than a whole set of features from a data point.\n"
"- $n$ qubits are required for $N$ data features, where $n\\leq N$. Often equality holds, here. We'll see how $n<N$ is possible in the next few sections.\n"
"- The resulting circuit is a constant depth (typically the depth is 1 prior to transpilation).\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengekodan sudut berbeza daripada dua kaedah sebelumnya dalam beberapa cara. Dalam pengekodan sudut:\n"
"- Setiap nilai ciri dipetakan ke qubit yang sepadan, $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k \\rightarrow Q_k$, meninggalkan qubit dalam keadaan produk.\n"
"- Satu nilai berangka dikodkan pada satu masa, bukan keseluruhan set ciri dari satu titik data.\n"
"- $n$ qubit diperlukan untuk $N$ ciri data, di mana $n\\leq N$. Selalunya kesamaan berlaku di sini. Kita akan lihat bagaimana $n<N$ mungkin dalam beberapa bahagian berikutnya.\n"
"- Litar kuantum yang terhasil mempunyai kedalaman tetap (biasanya kedalaman ialah 1 sebelum transpilasi).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The constant depth quantum circuit makes it particularly amenable to current quantum hardware. One additional feature of encoding our data using $\\theta$ (and specifically, our choice to use Y-axis angle encoding) is that it creates real-valued quantum states that can be useful for certain applications. For Y-axis rotation, data is mapped with a Y-axis rotation gate $R_Y(\\theta)$ by a real-valued angle $\\theta \\in (0, 2\\pi]$ ([Qiskit RYGate](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.RYGate)). As with phase encoding (see below), we recommend that you rescale data so that $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k \\in (0,2\\pi]$, preventing information loss and other unwanted effects.\n"
msgstr "Litar kuantum berkedalaman tetap menjadikannya amat sesuai untuk perkakasan kuantum semasa. Satu ciri tambahan daripada pengekodan data kita menggunakan $\\theta$ (dan khususnya, pilihan kita untuk menggunakan pengekodan sudut paksi-Y) ialah ia mencipta keadaan kuantum bernilai nyata yang berguna untuk aplikasi tertentu. Untuk putaran paksi-Y, data dipetakan dengan get putaran paksi-Y $R_Y(\\theta)$ melalui sudut bernilai nyata $\\theta \\in (0, 2\\pi]$ ([Qiskit RYGate](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.RYGate)). Seperti pengekodan fasa (lihat di bawah), kami mengesyorkan anda menskalakan data semula supaya $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k \\in (0,2\\pi]$, mengelakkan kehilangan maklumat dan kesan-kesan lain yang tidak diingini.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following Qiskit code rotates a single qubit from an initial state $|0\\rangle$ to encode a data value $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k=\\frac{1}{2}\\pi$.\n"
msgstr "Kod Qiskit berikut memutar satu qubit dari keadaan awal $|0\\rangle$ untuk mengekodkan nilai data $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k=\\frac{1}{2}\\pi$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will define a function to visualize the action on the state vector. The details of the function definition are not important, but the ability to visualize the state vectors and their changes is important.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan mentakrifkan fungsi untuk menggambarkan tindakan ke atas vektor keadaan. Butiran definisi fungsi tidak penting, tetapi keupayaan untuk menggambarkan vektor keadaan dan perubahannya adalah penting.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-machine-learning/data-encoding/extracted-outputs/666700f7-7798-43ce-a8ca-d91e48adda4f-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-machine-learning/data-encoding/extracted-outputs/666700f7-7798-43ce-a8ca-d91e48adda4f-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That was just a single feature of a single data vector. When encoding $N$ features into the rotation angles of $n$ qubits, say for the $j^\\text{th}$ data vector $\\vec{x}^{(j)} = (x_1,...,x_N),$ the encoded product state will look like this:\n"
msgstr "Itu hanyalah satu ciri dari satu vektor data. Apabila mengekodkan $N$ ciri ke dalam sudut putaran $n$ qubit, katakan untuk vektor data ke-$j$ $\\vec{x}^{(j)} = (x_1,...,x_N),$ keadaan produk yang dikodkan akan kelihatan seperti ini:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\vec{x}^{(j)}\\rangle = \\bigotimes^N_{k=1} \\cos(\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|0\\rangle + \\sin(\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\vec{x}^{(j)}\\rangle = \\bigotimes^N_{k=1} \\cos(\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|0\\rangle + \\sin(\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We note that this is equivalent to\n"
msgstr "Kami perhatikan bahawa ini setara dengan\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\vec{x}^{(j)}\\rangle = \\bigotimes^N_{k=1} R_Y(2\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|0\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\vec{x}^{(j)}\\rangle = \\bigotimes^N_{k=1} R_Y(2\\vec{x}^{(j)}_k)|0\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-2}"
msgstr "Uji kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-2}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Encode the data vector $\\vec{x} = (0, \\pi/4, \\pi/2)$ using angle encoding, as described above.\n"
msgstr "Kodkan vektor data $\\vec{x} = (0, \\pi/4, \\pi/2)$ menggunakan pengekodan sudut, seperti yang diterangkan di atas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
